      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Merrittstown spans Luzerne and Redstone townships in Fayette County and has no independent municipal government of its own.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/merrittstown_pennsylvania",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Soils here are silty loam and clay loam from weathered shale and sandstone, supporting crops while echoing historic coal‑mining impacts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/merrittstown_pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Low‑lying valleys host small streams that can flood during heavy rains, a risk highlighted by Fayette County flash‑flood events.",
